####################################################################################################################################
# A .gitignore file specifies intentionally untracked files that Git shouldn't track by default. Each line in a .gitignore file    #
# specifies a pseudo-regex pattern. Any file with path and name matching the pattern is not tracked by default, although you can   #
# still manually add and track ignored files.                                                                                      #
#                                                                                                                                  #
# Full documentation about .gitignore: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitignore                                                          #
#                                                                                                                                  #
# Copyright © 2026 Maneuver Games LLC. All rights reserved.                                                                        #
####################################################################################################################################

# For Visual Studio Code projects to ignore temporary files, build results, and files generated by popular add-ons.
# Not to be confused with Visual Studio, which is a different IDE.
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/VisualStudio.gitignore
# Workspace config delegated here from root.

# Workspace config and state, most of which is user-specific and should not be shared.
./*

# ...Except for the following files, which are project-specific and should be shared.
!**/*.code-snippets
!**/*.code-workspace
!**/*.shproj
!**/extensions.json
!**/launch.json
!**/settings.json
!**/tasks.json
